<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmad Shah Bahadur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1725">1725</a>–<a href="/years/1775">1775</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmad Shah Bahadur was Mughal emperor from 1748 to 1754, the son of Muhammad Shah. His reign saw the empire lose the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-abdali">Ahmad Shah Durrani</a> and suffer raids by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a>, while power at court lay with ministers and his mother. In 1754 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi-ud-din-khan-imad-ul-mulk">Ghazi-ud-din Khan Imad-ul-Mulk</a> deposed and blinded him, and he lived in captivity until his death in 1775.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-bahadur.jpg" alt="Ahmad Shah Bahadur" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gurkan1526 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AhmadShah.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
